## 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE & OVERVIEW

The objective of this engagement is to design, develop, deploy, and scale a specialized mobile fintech wallet application purpose-built for commercial transport drivers (cabs, interstate buses, tricycles, dispatch riders, and haulage truckers).

In the Nigerian cash-to-digital mobility landscape, commercial drivers face major operational friction with bank transfers:
* Traditional personal bank accounts fail to deliver immediate alerts while driving.
* Drivers waste time waiting for bank SMS alerts or asking passengers to show debit screens, leading to arguments, traffic blockages, and vulnerability to fake transfer receipts.
* Mixing personal finances with daily operating cash creates accounting chaos for fleet managers and transport unions.

This platform solves these challenges by automatically provisioning every driver with a unique, dedicated Nigerian bank account number (dynamic NUBAN via Paystack Dedicated Virtual Accounts, Monnify, or Moniepoint Microfinance Bank) registered in their name.

When a passenger sends money via instant bank transfer, the driver's in-app wallet is credited in real time via sub-second cloud webhooks, triggering an immediate loud audio chime and spoken voice credit alert so the driver confirms payment safely while operating the vehicle.

